Adaptations / environment
The public stream constructor accepts zero and sub-token budgets and fails with OutputExhausted when a token is first requested. Cargo emitted macOS SDK discovery/Xcode cache warnings during the initial test build; build and tests succeeded. All Cargo commands were locked and offline. No dependency, toolchain component, or network access was added.
Implemented WO-RUST-XML-STORAGE-01 in the XML stream. Token growth now uses bounded exact reservations, with checks against retained `Vec` capacity. Added storage accessors for tokens and the open-name stack, and preserved count-based `with_limits` semantics. Zero and sub-token budgets now report `OutputExhausted` at the first token’s offset.

Added boundary and lifecycle regressions in [stream_tests.rs](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/.worktrees/rust-xml-storage/rust/crates/vexel-xml/src/stream_tests.rs). The implementation is in [stream.rs](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/.worktrees/rust-xml-storage/rust/crates/vexel-xml/src/stream.rs).

Verification passed: Rust 1.99 check, all 31 XML tests, work-order validation, ledger validation (1,222 entries), and `git diff --check`. Evidence is in [result.md](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/.worktrees/rust-xml-storage/artifacts/WO-RUST-XML-STORAGE-01/result.md), [parity-map.json](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/.worktrees/rust-xml-storage/artifacts/WO-RUST-XML-STORAGE-01/parity-map.json), and [verification.txt](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/.worktrees/rust-xml-storage/artifacts/WO-RUST-XML-STORAGE-01/verification.txt).

